(1080,12,N'ZH-ZY-2-10 · 幫助新同學（中級）',N'今天，班上來了一位新同學。我把今天的事情說給朋友聽，他也分享自己的經驗。老師介紹他的名字，請大家和他問好。我帶他看看教室，也告訴他書本放在哪裡。我想把今天的發現告訴家人。我們再試一次。下課時，他站在座位旁邊，不知道可以做什麼。',0,N'intermediate',0),
(1081,12,N'ZH-ZY-3-01 · 早晨上學（高級）',N'早上，我先洗臉，再和家人吃早餐。媽媽提醒我帶水杯，我把它放進書包。我把今天的事情說給朋友聽，他也分享自己的經驗。我說：「我想再試一次！」出門時，天空很亮，路旁的小樹隨風搖動。我在路口等綠燈，確認車子停下才過馬路。

到了學校，同學正在整理桌子。我放好書包，拿出課本，準備開始今天的學習。今天值日的同學先打開窗戶，讓新鮮空氣進來。老師請我們分享早上發現的小事，有人看見鳥，有人幫忙收好碗。輪到我時，我說自己記得帶水杯。老師笑著說，每天做好一件小事，就能慢慢養成好習慣。這個小小的發現，讓普通的一天變得有趣。

我也說出自己的想法。我們不急著完成每一件事。我仔細看了看身邊的環境。事情做好以後，我的心情也變好了。今天我學到新的事情。我們先做好準備，再開始行動。下課後，我和朋友約好，明天也要準時到校。',0,N'advanced',0),
(1082,12,N'ZH-ZY-3-02 · 公園散步（高級）',N'星期天，我和家人到公園散步。小路兩旁有大樹，樹下有幾片落葉。我先聽清楚朋友說的話，再回答他的問題。我說：「我想再試一次！」我們走到水池邊，看見小魚在水裡游來游去。弟弟想跑近一點，爸爸提醒他慢慢走。我們坐下喝水，聽見鳥在樹上唱歌。

回家以前，大家一起把垃圾帶走，讓公園保持乾淨。我發現不同的葉子有不同的形狀，有的細長，有的像小手。媽媽讓我用眼睛仔細看，不要把樹上的葉子摘下來。後來，幾個孩子走來玩球，我們就把小路讓出來。這個小小的發現，讓普通的一天變得有趣。大家笑了。我想把今天的發現告訴家人。

大家一起想辦法。我仔細看了看身邊的環境。今天我學到新的事情。我們再試一次。我把這件事記在本子上。大家輪流分享，沒有人急著搶話。大家都有自己的活動，只要留意別人的位置，就能一起享受公園的好時光。',0,N'advanced',0),
(1083,12,N'ZH-ZY-3-03 · 圖書館借書（高級）',N'放學後，我到圖書館找一本故事書。書架上有許多書，我先看封面，再讀幾行介紹。我問家人這件事該怎麼做，聽完以後再試一次。我說：「我想再試一次！」找到喜歡的書以後，我坐下來安靜閱讀。故事中的小孩遇到困難，朋友一起想辦法幫忙。我把借書日期記在本子上，也記得看還書日期。

回家後，我想把故事說給妹妹聽。讀到不懂的地方，我先看看前後的句子，再向老師請教。老師沒有立刻給答案，而是請我說出自己的想法。我慢慢發現，圖片和文字可以一起幫助理解故事。借書時，我用雙手把書放好，沒有折起書角。大家笑了。我也說出自己的想法。

這讓我很開心。我把這件事記在本子上。這個小小的發現，讓普通的一天變得有趣。今天我學到新的事情。朋友認真聽我說。我仔細看了看身邊的環境。大家一起想辦法。下次來，我還想找一本介紹動物的書。',0,N'advanced',0),
(1084,12,N'ZH-ZY-3-04 · 準備午餐（高級）',N'中午，我和家人一起準備午餐。爸爸煮飯，媽媽洗菜，我幫忙把碗和筷子放好。我把今天的事情說給朋友聽，他也分享自己的經驗。我說：「我想再試一次！」妹妹洗好手，坐在椅子上等大家。我們吃飯時，說說今天有趣的事情。

吃完以後，我把碗放到水槽旁邊，再擦乾淨桌子。大家一起分工，很快就把廚房整理好了。媽媽教我先看清楚需要的東西，再一樣一樣拿出來。切菜和使用熱水的工作交給大人，我只做自己能安全完成的事。飯菜上桌時，大家先等家人坐好。我試著把每一種菜都吃一點，也不拿超過自己需要的份量。我也說出自己的想法。

今天我學到新的事情。我們先做好準備，再開始行動。這個小小的發現，讓普通的一天變得有趣。事情做好以後，我的心情也變好了。大人提醒我留意安全。我們不急著完成每一件事。剩下的食物收好，下次就不會浪費。',0,N'advanced',0),
(1085,12,N'ZH-ZY-3-05 · 雨天回家（高級）',N'放學時，天空開始下雨。我穿好雨衣，把書包放在雨衣裡面。我先聽清楚朋友說的話，再回答他的問題。我說：「我想再試一次！」路上有一些積水，我慢慢走，不急著跳過水面。到了路口，我先停下來看車子。爸爸在門口等我，手裡拿著乾毛巾。

回到家，我換好鞋子和衣服，才坐下喝水。窗外的雨聲聽起來像一首小歌。我原本想和朋友在門口多聊一會兒，但雨越下越大。我們先說好明天再分享故事，今天各自平安回家。爸爸提醒我，雨傘不能擋住前方的視線。我把傘收好，放在不會讓人跌倒的地方。這讓我很開心。

我們先做好準備，再開始行動。這個小小的發現，讓普通的一天變得有趣。我們不急著完成每一件事。我們再試一次。我仔細看了看身邊的環境。我想把今天的發現告訴家人。我把這件事記在本子上。衣服整理好以後，我也檢查課本有沒有被雨水弄溼。',0,N'advanced',0),
(1086,12,N'ZH-ZY-3-06 · 種一盆小花（高級）',N'老師送給每人一顆種子。我把種子放進花盆，蓋上一些土，再加一點水。我問家人這件事該怎麼做，聽完以後再試一次。我說：「我想再試一次！」每天早上，我到窗邊看看花盆，記錄有沒有變化。幾天以後，一片小葉子從土裡長出來。我很開心，卻沒有用手去拉它。

媽媽說，植物需要時間生長，只要好好照顧，就能看見新的變化。我在本子上畫下葉子的樣子，也寫上當天的日期。有一天，我發現土還是溼的，就沒有再加水。我請老師幫忙看看，知道水不是越多越好。朋友的植物長得比我的高，我也不著急。我們先做好準備，再開始行動。我慢慢看。我把這件事記在本子上。

這讓我很開心。大家一起想辦法。我也說出自己的想法。我仔細看了看身邊的環境。大家笑了。我記住了。我想把今天的發現告訴家人。每一盆植物都有自己的變化，仔細觀察比只看高度更有意思。',0,N'advanced',0),
(1087,12,N'ZH-ZY-3-07 · 整理自己的房間（高級）',N'星期六，我決定整理自己的房間。我先把書放回書架，再把玩具分成幾類。我把今天的事情說給朋友聽，他也分享自己的經驗。我說：「我想再試一次！」常玩的玩具放在容易拿到的盒子裡，其他的收進箱子。媽媽幫我擦高處的灰塵，我負責整理書桌。收好以後，地板多出一片空間。

我坐下來讀書，覺得房間比以前明亮，也更舒服。整理時，我找到一本很久沒有讀的書，差點忘記原本要做的事。我先把書放在桌角，等工作完成再看。盒子外面寫上名字，就能清楚知道裡面放什麼。弟弟來找玩具時，我請他用完放回原位。大家輪流分享，沒有人急著搶話。這個小小的發現，讓普通的一天變得有趣。

今天我學到新的事情。大家一起想辦法。大家笑了。朋友認真聽我說。這讓我很開心。我也說出自己的想法。只要每天花一點時間收好東西，就不用等到房間很亂才整理。',0,N'advanced',0),
(1088,12,N'ZH-ZY-3-08 · 一起玩球（高級）',N'下課後，我們到操場玩球。大家先說好規則，再分成兩隊。我先聽清楚朋友說的話，再回答他的問題。我說：「我想再試一次！」我把球傳給朋友，他接住以後，又傳給另一位同學。有一次，我沒有接到球，心裡有點難過。朋友說可以再試一次，我就深呼吸，重新站好。

遊戲結束時，大家一起收球，也謝謝彼此的幫忙。老師提醒我們，傳球前要先看看對方有沒有準備好。我試著放慢動作，把方向看清楚。後來，有位同學想加入，我們就調整隊伍，讓每個人都有機會。比分不是唯一重要的事，能一起合作也很開心。我們再試一次。大家一起想辦法。

今天我學到新的事情。我們不急著完成每一件事。我把這件事記在本子上。我仔細看了看身邊的環境。我想把今天的發現告訴家人。這個小小的發現，讓普通的一天變得有趣。休息時，大家到陰影下喝水，再決定要不要繼續練習。',0,N'advanced',0),
(1089,12,N'ZH-ZY-3-09 · 到市場買水果（高級）',N'早上，我和爸爸到市場買水果。我們先想好需要的數量，再看看不同攤位的價格。我問家人這件事該怎麼做，聽完以後再試一次。我說：「我想再試一次！」爸爸挑了幾顆蘋果，我選了一串香蕉。老闆把水果放進我們帶來的袋子，還提醒香蕉要輕輕拿。

我幫忙看好袋子，爸爸負責付錢。回家以後，我們把水果洗乾淨，分給家人一起吃。市場裡的人很多，我跟在爸爸旁邊，不離開他的視線。我發現有些水果的大小不同，就問爸爸該怎麼選。爸爸說，先想清楚用途，不一定要挑最大的一個。我們沒有因為便宜就買太多，免得吃不完。

這個小小的發現，讓普通的一天變得有趣。我想把今天的發現告訴家人。我們再試一次。我也說出自己的想法。大家輪流分享，沒有人急著搶話。我們先做好準備，再開始行動。這次買東西讓我知道，出門以前做好準備，可以省下不少時間。',0,N'advanced',0),
(1090,12,N'ZH-ZY-3-10 · 幫助新同學（高級）',N'今天，班上來了一位新同學。老師介紹他的名字，請大家和他問好。我把今天的事情說給朋友聽，他也分享自己的經驗。我說：「我想再試一次！」我帶他看看教室，也告訴他書本放在哪裡。下課時，他站在座位旁邊，不知道可以做什麼。

我邀請他一起到操場玩，其他朋友也走過來介紹自己。放學以前，他笑著說，明天還想和我們一起玩。午餐時，我先問他想坐在哪裡，沒有替他做決定。他說自己喜歡畫畫，我就介紹也喜歡畫畫的朋友給他認識。有些班上的規則他還不清楚，我慢慢說明，讓他有時間發問。我發現，幫忙不只是說很多話，也要聽見別人的需要。

我想把今天的發現告訴家人。事情做好以後，我的心情也變好了。我們不急著完成每一件事。我們再試一次。今天我學到新的事情。大家輪流分享，沒有人急著搶話。大家互相了解，教室就更像一個溫暖的家。',0,N'advanced',0),
(1091,13,N'EN-1-01 · A School Morning（初級）',N'I get up when the sky is light. I wash my face and put on my clothes. My bag is next to the door. I check my book and my water bottle. We eat breakfast together. I walk to school with Dad. We talk. Now I am ready to learn.',0,N'beginner',0),
(1092,13,N'EN-1-02 · A Walk in the Park（初級）',N'We go to the park on Sunday. The path is wide and clean. I see a tall tree and some small flowers. A bird sits on a branch. My little brother points at the pond. We stand back and watch the fish. I try again. Dad gives us some water.',0,N'beginner',0),
(1093,13,N'EN-1-03 · My Library Book（初級）',N'I visit the library after school. There are many books on the shelves. I look for a story about a small animal. The cover has a bright picture. I read a few lines before I choose it. We make a plan. Then I sit at a table and read quietly.',0,N'beginner',0),
(1094,13,N'EN-1-04 · Lunch at Home（初級）',N'We make lunch together at home. Dad cooks the rice and Mom washes the vegetables. I put bowls and spoons on the table. My sister washes her hands before she sits down. We wait until everyone is ready. We learn something new today. At lunch, we talk about our day.',0,N'beginner',0),
(1095,13,N'EN-1-05 · A Rainy Day（初級）',N'It starts to rain when school ends. I put on my raincoat and keep my bag dry. There is water on the path. I walk slowly and watch where I step. At the road, I stop and look for cars. I try again. Dad waits for me near our door.',0,N'beginner',0),
(1096,13,N'EN-1-06 · A Seed in a Pot（初級）',N'My teacher gives me a seed. I put it in a pot and cover it with soil. Then I add a little water. The pot sits near a window. Every morning, I look for a change. My friend listens. I try again. One day, a small green leaf comes out.',0,N'beginner',0),
(1097,13,N'EN-1-07 · A Tidy Room（初級）',N'I want to make my room tidy. First I put my books on the shelf. Then I sort my toys into boxes. The toys I use often are easy to reach. Mom helps clean the high places. I take my time. I smile. I wipe my desk with a cloth.',0,N'beginner',0),
(1098,13,N'EN-1-08 · A Game with Friends（初級）',N'We play with a ball after class. First we agree on the rules. Then we make two teams. I pass the ball to my friend. She catches it and passes it to another child. We talk. My friend listens. We feel happy. Once I miss the ball and feel sad.',0,N'beginner',0),
(1099,13,N'EN-1-09 · Fruit at the Market（初級）',N'Dad and I go to the market. We bring our own bag. First we think about how much fruit we need. I see red apples and yellow bananas. Dad checks the prices at two stands. My friend listens. We feel happy. We choose fruit that we can finish at home.',0,N'beginner',0),
(1100,13,N'EN-1-10 · A New Classmate（初級）',N'A new child joins our class today. Our teacher tells us his name. I say hello and show him his seat. I tell him where we keep our books. At break time, he looks unsure about what to do. We rest. I ask if he wants to play with us.',0,N'beginner',0),
(1101,13,N'EN-2-01 · A School Morning（中級）',N'I get up when the sky is light. I wash my face and put on my clothes. My bag is next to the door. I check my book and my water bottle. We eat breakfast together. I walk to school with Dad. We stop before we cross the road. My friend waves to me at the gate. I put my bag beside my chair. Now I am ready to learn. Our teacher asks us to share one small thing from the morning. I tell her about a bird near our window. We talk. Thanks. We listen while each person speaks.',0,N'intermediate',0),
(1102,13,N'EN-2-02 · A Walk in the Park（中級）',N'We go to the park on Sunday. The path is wide and clean. I see a tall tree and some small flowers. A bird sits on a branch. My little brother points at the pond. We stand back and watch the fish. Dad gives us some water. We sit on a bench and rest. Before we leave, we put our trash in a bag. The park is a good place to spend time together. Some leaves are round and some are long. I look at them without picking them. We check our work together. We move to give them room.',0,N'intermediate',0),
(1103,13,N'EN-2-03 · My Library Book（中級）',N'I visit the library after school. There are many books on the shelves. I look for a story about a small animal. The cover has a bright picture. I read a few lines before I choose it. Then I sit at a table and read quietly. I use a small card to mark my page. I check when I must return the book. At home, I tell my sister about the story. One part of the story is hard to understand. We check our work together. We feel happy. I read the lines before it and look at the picture.',0,N'intermediate',0),
(1104,13,N'EN-2-04 · Lunch at Home（中級）',N'We make lunch together at home. Dad cooks the rice and Mom washes the vegetables. I put bowls and spoons on the table. My sister washes her hands before she sits down. We wait until everyone is ready. At lunch, we talk about our day. I try a little of each kind of food. After lunch, I help clean the table. We all have a small job to do. Hot water and sharp tools are for adults to use. I can carry a clean plate and fold a cloth. We feel happy. Dad puts the extra food away for later.',0,N'intermediate',0),
(1105,13,N'EN-2-05 · A Rainy Day（中級）',N'It starts to rain when school ends. I put on my raincoat and keep my bag dry. There is water on the path. I walk slowly and watch where I step. At the road, I stop and look for cars. Dad waits for me near our door. He has a dry towel in his hands. I change my wet shoes at home. Then I listen to the rain by the window. My friend wants to tell me a story, but the rain gets heavier. We decide to talk at school tomorrow. We rest. I check that my books are dry.',0,N'intermediate',0),
(1106,13,N'EN-2-06 · A Seed in a Pot（中級）',N'My teacher gives me a seed. I put it in a pot and cover it with soil. Then I add a little water. The pot sits near a window. Every morning, I look for a change. One day, a small green leaf comes out. I am happy to see it. I do not pull the plant. Mom says that it needs time to grow. I draw the leaf in my notebook. I write the date next to my drawing. We make a plan. I take my time. Sometimes the soil is still wet, so I do not add more water.',0,N'intermediate',0),
(1107,13,N'EN-2-07 · A Tidy Room（中級）',N'I want to make my room tidy. First I put my books on the shelf. Then I sort my toys into boxes. The toys I use often are easy to reach. Mom helps clean the high places. I wipe my desk with a cloth. There is more space on the floor now. I sit down with a book. The room feels bright and comfortable. I know where to find my things. While I work, I find an old storybook. I want to read it, but I finish my job first. We feel happy. At home, I think about what happened.',0,N'intermediate',0),
(1108,13,N'EN-2-08 · A Game with Friends（中級）',N'We play with a ball after class. First we agree on the rules. Then we make two teams. I pass the ball to my friend. She catches it and passes it to another child. Once I miss the ball and feel sad. My friend says that I can try again. I take a breath and stand ready. At the end, we put the ball away together. I thank my friends for the game. Before I pass, I check that my friend is ready. We feel happy. Thanks. I slow down and look at where I want the ball to go.',0,N'intermediate',0),
(1109,13,N'EN-2-09 · Fruit at the Market（中級）',N'Dad and I go to the market. We bring our own bag. First we think about how much fruit we need. I see red apples and yellow bananas. Dad checks the prices at two stands. We choose fruit that we can finish at home. I hold the bag while Dad pays. We thank the seller before we leave. At home, we wash the fruit and share it with our family. There are many people, so I stay close to Dad. I ask why some apples are bigger than others. We rest. A little planning helps us use our money well.',0,N'intermediate',0),
(1110,13,N'EN-2-10 · A New Classmate（中級）',N'A new child joins our class today. Our teacher tells us his name. I say hello and show him his seat. I tell him where we keep our books. At break time, he looks unsure about what to do. I ask if he wants to play with us. My friends introduce themselves too. At the end of the day, he smiles. He says that he wants to come back tomorrow. At lunch, I ask where he would like to sit. I listen instead of choosing for him. I take my time. Some of our class rules are new to him.',0,N'intermediate',0),
(1111,13,N'EN-3-01 · A School Morning（高級）',N'I get up when the sky is light. I wash my face and put on my clothes. My bag is next to the door. I check my book and my water bottle. We eat breakfast together. I walk to school with Dad. We stop before we cross the road. My friend waves to me at the gate. I put my bag beside my chair. Now I am ready to learn. Our teacher asks us to share one small thing from the morning. I tell her about a bird near our window. My friend tells us about his new shoes. We listen while each person speaks. After class, I help put the books in a neat pile. Small jobs are easier when we work together. I want to remember my water bottle again tomorrow. At home, I think about what happened. I write a few lines in my notebook. I put the events in order so that I can tell the story clearly. My family listens and asks what I learned. I explain the part that was easy and the part that was hard. We think of a small change that could help next time. I do not have to get everything right at once. Learning takes time, and I can improve by trying again. Before bed, I get ready for the next day. We talk. I tell my family about it. We help each other. There is no need to rush. We feel happy. My friend listens. A small job can teach me to be patient and to pay attention. I can use a picture to help me remember the order of the events. My family gives me time to explain what I have learned from this experience. I feel glad that I noticed something useful in an ordinary day.',0,N'advanced',0),
(1112,13,N'EN-3-02 · A Walk in the Park（高級）',N'We go to the park on Sunday. The path is wide and clean. I see a tall tree and some small flowers. A bird sits on a branch. My little brother points at the pond. We stand back and watch the fish. Dad gives us some water. We sit on a bench and rest. Before we leave, we put our trash in a bag. The park is a good place to spend time together. Some leaves are round and some are long. I look at them without picking them. A group of children wants to play with a ball. We move to give them room. Mom asks me what I like best. I say that I like the sound of the birds. We agree to come back on another day and see what has changed. At home, I think about what happened. I write a few lines in my notebook. I put the events in order so that I can tell the story clearly. My family listens and asks what I learned. I explain the part that was easy and the part that was hard. We think of a small change that could help next time. I do not have to get everything right at once. Learning takes time, and I can improve by trying again. Before bed, I get ready for the next day. My friend and I can have different ideas and still listen to each other. I notice that a careful plan can make a simple task easier for everyone. I remember this day. I do not need difficult words to tell other people about my day. We feel happy. We give each person a turn and make sure that no one feels left out. I feel glad that I noticed something useful in an ordinary day.',0,N'advanced',0),
(1113,13,N'EN-3-03 · My Library Book（高級）',N'I visit the library after school. There are many books on the shelves. I look for a story about a small animal. The cover has a bright picture. I read a few lines before I choose it. Then I sit at a table and read quietly. I use a small card to mark my page. I check when I must return the book. At home, I tell my sister about the story. One part of the story is hard to understand. I read the lines before it and look at the picture. My teacher asks me to explain what I think. Her question helps me find an answer. I do not fold the corners of the pages. I keep the book away from food and water. Next time, I want to find a book about trees. At home, I think about what happened. I write a few lines in my notebook. I put the events in order so that I can tell the story clearly. My family listens and asks what I learned. I explain the part that was easy and the part that was hard. We think of a small change that could help next time. I do not have to get everything right at once. Learning takes time, and I can improve by trying again. Before bed, I get ready for the next day. We talk. When I am not sure what to do, I can ask someone who knows. There is no need to rush. We learn something new today. Thanks. The next time I try, I will remember to stop and think before I act. I try again. My friend listens. I tell my family about it. I want to try this again tomorrow. I feel glad that I noticed something useful in an ordinary day.',0,N'advanced',0),
(1114,13,N'EN-3-04 · Lunch at Home（高級）',N'We make lunch together at home. Dad cooks the rice and Mom washes the vegetables. I put bowls and spoons on the table. My sister washes her hands before she sits down. We wait until everyone is ready. At lunch, we talk about our day. I try a little of each kind of food. After lunch, I help clean the table. We all have a small job to do. Hot water and sharp tools are for adults to use. I can carry a clean plate and fold a cloth. Mom shows me how to put things where they belong. We take only as much food as we can eat. Dad puts the extra food away for later. I thank my family for the meal. Working together makes the room neat again. At home, I think about what happened. I write a few lines in my notebook. I put the events in order so that I can tell the story clearly. My family listens and asks what I learned. I explain the part that was easy and the part that was hard. We think of a small change that could help next time. I do not have to get everything right at once. Learning takes time, and I can improve by trying again. Before bed, I get ready for the next day. I take my time. I keep my notes in a safe place so that I can find them later. I do not need difficult words to tell other people about my day. The next time I try, I will remember to stop and think before I act. I smile. We feel happy. I ask a simple question. We help each other. I tell my family about it. I feel glad that I noticed something useful in an ordinary day.',0,N'advanced',0),
(1115,13,N'EN-3-05 · A Rainy Day（高級）',N'It starts to rain when school ends. I put on my raincoat and keep my bag dry. There is water on the path. I walk slowly and watch where I step. At the road, I stop and look for cars. Dad waits for me near our door. He has a dry towel in his hands. I change my wet shoes at home. Then I listen to the rain by the window. My friend wants to tell me a story, but the rain gets heavier. We decide to talk at school tomorrow. I hold my umbrella so that I can see in front of me. At home, I put it where no one will trip over it. I check that my books are dry. Dad says that getting home safely is more important than getting home quickly. At home, I think about what happened. I write a few lines in my notebook. I put the events in order so that I can tell the story clearly. My family listens and asks what I learned. I explain the part that was easy and the part that was hard. We think of a small change that could help next time. I do not have to get everything right at once. Learning takes time, and I can improve by trying again. Before bed, I get ready for the next day. I take my time. I tell my family about it. I remember this day. We give each person a turn and make sure that no one feels left out. My family gives me time to explain what I have learned from this experience. There is no need to rush. I do not need difficult words to tell other people about my day. I feel glad that I noticed something useful in an ordinary day.',0,N'advanced',0),
(1116,13,N'EN-3-06 · A Seed in a Pot（高級）',N'My teacher gives me a seed. I put it in a pot and cover it with soil. Then I add a little water. The pot sits near a window. Every morning, I look for a change. One day, a small green leaf comes out. I am happy to see it. I do not pull the plant. Mom says that it needs time to grow. I draw the leaf in my notebook. I write the date next to my drawing. Sometimes the soil is still wet, so I do not add more water. My teacher helps me learn what the plant needs. My friend has a taller plant, but I do not need to hurry mine. We compare our drawings and talk about the new leaves. Watching a small change can be very interesting. At home, I think about what happened. I write a few lines in my notebook. I put the events in order so that I can tell the story clearly. My family listens and asks what I learned. I explain the part that was easy and the part that was hard. We think of a small change that could help next time. I do not have to get everything right at once. Learning takes time, and I can improve by trying again. Before bed, I get ready for the next day. The next time I try, I will remember to stop and think before I act. We check our work together. We rest. We help each other. I look around me. We give each person a turn and make sure that no one feels left out. I keep my notes in a safe place so that I can find them later. I ask a simple question. I feel glad that I noticed something useful in an ordinary day.',0,N'advanced',0),
(1117,13,N'EN-3-07 · A Tidy Room（高級）',N'I want to make my room tidy. First I put my books on the shelf. Then I sort my toys into boxes. The toys I use often are easy to reach. Mom helps clean the high places. I wipe my desk with a cloth. There is more space on the floor now. I sit down with a book. The room feels bright and comfortable. I know where to find my things. While I work, I find an old storybook. I want to read it, but I finish my job first. I write names on the boxes to show what is inside. My brother borrows a toy and puts it back when he is done. Keeping things in order takes a little time each day. That is easier than waiting until the whole room is messy. At home, I think about what happened. I write a few lines in my notebook. I put the events in order so that I can tell the story clearly. My family listens and asks what I learned. I explain the part that was easy and the part that was hard. We think of a small change that could help next time. I do not have to get everything right at once. Learning takes time, and I can improve by trying again. Before bed, I get ready for the next day. I want to try this again tomorrow. I can use a picture to help me remember the order of the events. There is no need to rush. We give each person a turn and make sure that no one feels left out. We feel happy. We check our work together. I do not need difficult words to tell other people about my day. I feel glad that I noticed something useful in an ordinary day.',0,N'advanced',0),
(1118,13,N'EN-3-08 · A Game with Friends（高級）',N'We play with a ball after class. First we agree on the rules. Then we make two teams. I pass the ball to my friend. She catches it and passes it to another child. Once I miss the ball and feel sad. My friend says that I can try again. I take a breath and stand ready. At the end, we put the ball away together. I thank my friends for the game. Before I pass, I check that my friend is ready. I slow down and look at where I want the ball to go. Another child asks to join us. We change the teams so everyone can play. Winning is fun, but helping each other is fun too. We stop for water in the shade. Then we decide whether to play again. At home, I think about what happened. I write a few lines in my notebook. I put the events in order so that I can tell the story clearly. My family listens and asks what I learned. I explain the part that was easy and the part that was hard. We think of a small change that could help next time. I do not have to get everything right at once. Learning takes time, and I can improve by trying again. Before bed, I get ready for the next day. I look around me. I do not need difficult words to tell other people about my day. We make a plan. I notice that a careful plan can make a simple task easier for everyone. I can use a picture to help me remember the order of the events. We give each person a turn and make sure that no one feels left out. I feel glad that I noticed something useful in an ordinary day.',0,N'advanced',0),
(1119,13,N'EN-3-09 · Fruit at the Market（高級）',N'Dad and I go to the market. We bring our own bag. First we think about how much fruit we need. I see red apples and yellow bananas. Dad checks the prices at two stands. We choose fruit that we can finish at home. I hold the bag while Dad pays. We thank the seller before we leave. At home, we wash the fruit and share it with our family. There are many people, so I stay close to Dad. I ask why some apples are bigger than others. Dad says that the biggest one is not always the best choice for us. We do not buy too much just because the price is low. A little planning helps us use our money well. I want to help make the shopping list next time. At home, I think about what happened. I write a few lines in my notebook. I put the events in order so that I can tell the story clearly. My family listens and asks what I learned. I explain the part that was easy and the part that was hard. We think of a small change that could help next time. I do not have to get everything right at once. Learning takes time, and I can improve by trying again. Before bed, I get ready for the next day. A small job can teach me to be patient and to pay attention. When I am not sure what to do, I can ask someone who knows. I can use a picture to help me remember the order of the events. We feel happy. We make a plan. I look around me. I tell my family about it. There is no need to rush. I feel glad that I noticed something useful in an ordinary day.',0,N'advanced',0),
(1120,13,N'EN-3-10 · A New Classmate（高級）',N'A new child joins our class today. Our teacher tells us his name. I say hello and show him his seat. I tell him where we keep our books. At break time, he looks unsure about what to do. I ask if he wants to play with us. My friends introduce themselves too. At the end of the day, he smiles. He says that he wants to come back tomorrow. At lunch, I ask where he would like to sit. I listen instead of choosing for him. He likes to draw, so I tell him about a friend who likes drawing too. Some of our class rules are new to him. I explain them slowly and give him time to ask questions. Helping someone means listening as well as talking. At home, I think about what happened. I write a few lines in my notebook. I put the events in order so that I can tell the story clearly. My family listens and asks what I learned. I explain the part that was easy and the part that was hard. We think of a small change that could help next time. I do not have to get everything right at once. Learning takes time, and I can improve by trying again. Before bed, I get ready for the next day. My friend and I can have different ideas and still listen to each other. We check our work together. We talk. I ask a simple question. I do not need difficult words to tell other people about my day. There is no need to rush. We learn something new today. My family gives me time to explain what I have learned from this experience. I take my time. I feel glad that I noticed something useful in an ordinary day.',0,N'advanced',0),
(1121,14,N'ZH-LONG-01-P1 · 第1段',N'早上，我先洗臉，再和家人吃早餐。媽媽提醒我帶水杯，我把它放進書包。出門時，天空很亮，路旁的小樹隨風搖動。我在路口等綠燈，確認車子停下才過馬路。到了學校，同學正在整理桌子。我放好書包，拿出課本，準備開始今天的學習。今天值日的同學先打開窗戶，讓新鮮空氣進來。老師請我們分享早上發現的小事，有人看見鳥，有人幫忙收好碗。輪到我時，我說自己記得帶水杯。老師笑著說，每天做好一件小事，就能慢慢養成好習慣。大家一起想辦法。我想把今天的發現告訴家人。我記住了。我把早晨上學的經過記在本子上，想想哪裡做得好，哪裡可以再改進。大家輪流分享，沒有人急著搶話。我沒有急著回答，而是照著事情發生的順序慢慢回想。原來，只要多留意一點，就能在日常生活裡找到值得記住的小事。下課後，我和朋友約好，明天也要準時到校。',0,N'advanced',0),
(1122,14,N'ZH-LONG-01-P2 · 第2段',N'今天值日的同學先打開窗戶，讓新鮮空氣進來。老師請我們分享早上發現的小事，有人看見鳥，有人幫忙收好碗。輪到我時，我說自己記得帶水杯。老師笑著說，每天做好一件小事，就能慢慢養成好習慣。下課後，我和朋友約好，明天也要準時到校。我把早晨上學的經過記在本子上，想想哪裡做得好，哪裡可以再改進。家人聽完以後，請我先說說最難忘的地方。我沒有急著回答，而是照著事情發生的順序慢慢回想。原來，只要多留意一點，就能在日常生活裡找到值得記住的小事。後來，我和朋友討論遇到問題時可以怎麼做。我們先把不同的想法說出來，再看看哪些方法適合當時的情況。有些事情需要大人的協助，有些小事則可以自己練習。大人提醒我留意安全。大家一起想辦法。我們再試一次。大家不一定有相同的答案，但都願意聽完別人的理由。',0,N'advanced',0),
(1123,14,N'ZH-LONG-01-P3 · 第3段',N'幾天以後，我又想起早晨上學的經驗。這次，我先準備好需要的東西，也提醒自己留意安全。朋友問我為什麼這樣做，我就把前一次學到的事情說給他聽。我們一起試著安排順序，遇到不清楚的地方就先停下來討論。今天值日的同學先打開窗戶，讓新鮮空氣進來。老師請我們分享早上發現的小事，有人看見鳥，有人幫忙收好碗。輪到我時，我說自己記得帶水杯。老師笑著說，每天做好一件小事，就能慢慢養成好習慣。下課後，我和朋友約好，明天也要準時到校。回家以後，我在本子上補了新的記錄。朋友認真聽我說。大家一起想辦法。我仔細看了看身邊的環境。事情做好以後，我的心情也變好了。大家輪流分享，沒有人急著搶話。這個小小的發現，讓普通的一天變得有趣。這些小小的進步讓我知道，練習不是一次就要做好，而是每次都比以前多懂一點。',0,N'advanced',0),
(1124,14,N'ZH-LONG-01 · 全文',N'早上，我先洗臉，再和家人吃早餐。媽媽提醒我帶水杯，我把它放進書包。出門時，天空很亮，路旁的小樹隨風搖動。我在路口等綠燈，確認車子停下才過馬路。到了學校，同學正在整理桌子。我放好書包，拿出課本，準備開始今天的學習。今天值日的同學先打開窗戶，讓新鮮空氣進來。老師請我們分享早上發現的小事，有人看見鳥，有人幫忙收好碗。輪到我時，我說自己記得帶水杯。老師笑著說，每天做好一件小事，就能慢慢養成好習慣。大家一起想辦法。我想把今天的發現告訴家人。我記住了。我把早晨上學的經過記在本子上，想想哪裡做得好，哪裡可以再改進。大家輪流分享，沒有人急著搶話。我沒有急著回答，而是照著事情發生的順序慢慢回想。原來，只要多留意一點，就能在日常生活裡找到值得記住的小事。下課後，我和朋友約好，明天也要準時到校。

今天值日的同學先打開窗戶，讓新鮮空氣進來。老師請我們分享早上發現的小事，有人看見鳥，有人幫忙收好碗。輪到我時，我說自己記得帶水杯。老師笑著說，每天做好一件小事，就能慢慢養成好習慣。下課後，我和朋友約好，明天也要準時到校。我把早晨上學的經過記在本子上，想想哪裡做得好，哪裡可以再改進。家人聽完以後，請我先說說最難忘的地方。我沒有急著回答，而是照著事情發生的順序慢慢回想。原來，只要多留意一點，就能在日常生活裡找到值得記住的小事。後來，我和朋友討論遇到問題時可以怎麼做。我們先把不同的想法說出來，再看看哪些方法適合當時的情況。有些事情需要大人的協助，有些小事則可以自己練習。大人提醒我留意安全。大家一起想辦法。我們再試一次。大家不一定有相同的答案，但都願意聽完別人的理由。

幾天以後，我又想起早晨上學的經驗。這次，我先準備好需要的東西，也提醒自己留意安全。朋友問我為什麼這樣做，我就把前一次學到的事情說給他聽。我們一起試著安排順序，遇到不清楚的地方就先停下來討論。今天值日的同學先打開窗戶，讓新鮮空氣進來。老師請我們分享早上發現的小事，有人看見鳥，有人幫忙收好碗。輪到我時，我說自己記得帶水杯。老師笑著說，每天做好一件小事，就能慢慢養成好習慣。下課後，我和朋友約好，明天也要準時到校。回家以後，我在本子上補了新的記錄。朋友認真聽我說。大家一起想辦法。我仔細看了看身邊的環境。事情做好以後，我的心情也變好了。大家輪流分享，沒有人急著搶話。這個小小的發現，讓普通的一天變得有趣。這些小小的進步讓我知道，練習不是一次就要做好，而是每次都比以前多懂一點。',0,N'advanced',0),
(1125,14,N'ZH-LONG-02-P1 · 第1段',N'星期天，我和家人到公園散步。小路兩旁有大樹，樹下有幾片落葉。我們走到水池邊，看見小魚在水裡游來游去。弟弟想跑近一點，爸爸提醒他慢慢走。我們坐下喝水，聽見鳥在樹上唱歌。回家以前，大家一起把垃圾帶走，讓公園保持乾淨。我發現不同的葉子有不同的形狀，有的細長，有的像小手。媽媽讓我用眼睛仔細看，不要把樹上的葉子摘下來。後來，幾個孩子走來玩球，我們就把小路讓出來。大家輪流分享，沒有人急著搶話。大家笑了。我把這件事記在本子上。我也說出自己的想法。這個小小的發現，讓普通的一天變得有趣。朋友認真聽我說。今天我學到新的事情。我把公園散步的經過記在本子上，想想哪裡做得好，哪裡可以再改進。家人聽完以後，請我先說說最難忘的地方。大家都有自己的活動，只要留意別人的位置，就能一起享受公園的好時光。',0,N'advanced',0),
(1126,14,N'ZH-LONG-02-P2 · 第2段',N'我發現不同的葉子有不同的形狀，有的細長，有的像小手。媽媽讓我用眼睛仔細看，不要把樹上的葉子摘下來。後來，幾個孩子走來玩球，我們就把小路讓出來。大家都有自己的活動，只要留意別人的位置，就能一起享受公園的好時光。我把公園散步的經過記在本子上，想想哪裡做得好，哪裡可以再改進。家人聽完以後，請我先說說最難忘的地方。我沒有急著回答，而是照著事情發生的順序慢慢回想。原來，只要多留意一點，就能在日常生活裡找到值得記住的小事。後來，我和朋友討論遇到問題時可以怎麼做。我們先把不同的想法說出來，再看看哪些方法適合當時的情況。有些事情需要大人的協助，有些小事則可以自己練習。大家一起想辦法。這讓我很開心。大家輪流分享，沒有人急著搶話。大家不一定有相同的答案，但都願意聽完別人的理由。',0,N'advanced',0),
(1127,14,N'ZH-LONG-02-P3 · 第3段',N'幾天以後，我又想起公園散步的經驗。這次，我先準備好需要的東西，也提醒自己留意安全。朋友問我為什麼這樣做，我就把前一次學到的事情說給他聽。我們一起試著安排順序，遇到不清楚的地方就先停下來討論。我發現不同的葉子有不同的形狀，有的細長，有的像小手。媽媽讓我用眼睛仔細看，不要把樹上的葉子摘下來。後來，幾個孩子走來玩球，我們就把小路讓出來。大家都有自己的活動，只要留意別人的位置，就能一起享受公園的好時光。回家以後，我在本子上補了新的記錄。我仔細看了看身邊的環境。我們不急著完成每一件事。我想把今天的發現告訴家人。我沒有急著回答，而是照著事情發生的順序慢慢回想。家人聽完以後，請我先說說最難忘的地方。這些小小的進步讓我知道，練習不是一次就要做好，而是每次都比以前多懂一點。',0,N'advanced',0),
(1128,14,N'ZH-LONG-02 · 全文',N'星期天，我和家人到公園散步。小路兩旁有大樹，樹下有幾片落葉。我們走到水池邊，看見小魚在水裡游來游去。弟弟想跑近一點，爸爸提醒他慢慢走。我們坐下喝水，聽見鳥在樹上唱歌。回家以前，大家一起把垃圾帶走，讓公園保持乾淨。我發現不同的葉子有不同的形狀，有的細長，有的像小手。媽媽讓我用眼睛仔細看，不要把樹上的葉子摘下來。後來，幾個孩子走來玩球，我們就把小路讓出來。大家輪流分享，沒有人急著搶話。大家笑了。我把這件事記在本子上。我也說出自己的想法。這個小小的發現，讓普通的一天變得有趣。朋友認真聽我說。今天我學到新的事情。我把公園散步的經過記在本子上，想想哪裡做得好，哪裡可以再改進。家人聽完以後，請我先說說最難忘的地方。大家都有自己的活動，只要留意別人的位置，就能一起享受公園的好時光。

我發現不同的葉子有不同的形狀，有的細長，有的像小手。媽媽讓我用眼睛仔細看，不要把樹上的葉子摘下來。後來，幾個孩子走來玩球，我們就把小路讓出來。大家都有自己的活動，只要留意別人的位置，就能一起享受公園的好時光。我把公園散步的經過記在本子上，想想哪裡做得好，哪裡可以再改進。家人聽完以後，請我先說說最難忘的地方。我沒有急著回答，而是照著事情發生的順序慢慢回想。原來，只要多留意一點，就能在日常生活裡找到值得記住的小事。後來，我和朋友討論遇到問題時可以怎麼做。我們先把不同的想法說出來，再看看哪些方法適合當時的情況。有些事情需要大人的協助，有些小事則可以自己練習。大家一起想辦法。這讓我很開心。大家輪流分享，沒有人急著搶話。大家不一定有相同的答案，但都願意聽完別人的理由。

幾天以後，我又想起公園散步的經驗。這次，我先準備好需要的東西，也提醒自己留意安全。朋友問我為什麼這樣做，我就把前一次學到的事情說給他聽。我們一起試著安排順序，遇到不清楚的地方就先停下來討論。我發現不同的葉子有不同的形狀，有的細長，有的像小手。媽媽讓我用眼睛仔細看，不要把樹上的葉子摘下來。後來，幾個孩子走來玩球，我們就把小路讓出來。大家都有自己的活動，只要留意別人的位置，就能一起享受公園的好時光。回家以後，我在本子上補了新的記錄。我仔細看了看身邊的環境。我們不急著完成每一件事。我想把今天的發現告訴家人。我沒有急著回答，而是照著事情發生的順序慢慢回想。家人聽完以後，請我先說說最難忘的地方。這些小小的進步讓我知道，練習不是一次就要做好，而是每次都比以前多懂一點。',0,N'advanced',0),
(1129,14,N'ZH-LONG-03-P1 · 第1段',N'放學後，我到圖書館找一本故事書。書架上有許多書，我先看封面，再讀幾行介紹。找到喜歡的書以後，我坐下來安靜閱讀。故事中的小孩遇到困難，朋友一起想辦法幫忙。我把借書日期記在本子上，也記得看還書日期。回家後，我想把故事說給妹妹聽。讀到不懂的地方，我先看看前後的句子，再向老師請教。老師沒有立刻給答案，而是請我說出自己的想法。我慢慢發現，圖片和文字可以一起幫助理解故事。借書時，我用雙手把書放好，沒有折起書角。我想把今天的發現告訴家人。這個小小的發現，讓普通的一天變得有趣。我把這件事記在本子上。大家一起想辦法。我慢慢看。我們不急著完成每一件事。我們再試一次。我仔細看了看身邊的環境。我把圖書館借書的經過記在本子上，想想哪裡做得好，哪裡可以再改進。下次來，我還想找一本介紹動物的書。',0,N'advanced',0),
(1130,14,N'ZH-LONG-03-P2 · 第2段',N'讀到不懂的地方，我先看看前後的句子，再向老師請教。老師沒有立刻給答案，而是請我說出自己的想法。我慢慢發現，圖片和文字可以一起幫助理解故事。借書時，我用雙手把書放好，沒有折起書角。下次來，我還想找一本介紹動物的書。我把圖書館借書的經過記在本子上，想想哪裡做得好，哪裡可以再改進。家人聽完以後，請我先說說最難忘的地方。我沒有急著回答，而是照著事情發生的順序慢慢回想。原來，只要多留意一點，就能在日常生活裡找到值得記住的小事。後來，我和朋友討論遇到問題時可以怎麼做。我們先把不同的想法說出來，再看看哪些方法適合當時的情況。有些事情需要大人的協助，有些小事則可以自己練習。書架上有許多書，我先看封面，再讀幾行介紹。這讓我很開心。大家不一定有相同的答案，但都願意聽完別人的理由。',0,N'advanced',0),
(1131,14,N'ZH-LONG-03-P3 · 第3段',N'幾天以後，我又想起圖書館借書的經驗。這次，我先準備好需要的東西，也提醒自己留意安全。朋友問我為什麼這樣做，我就把前一次學到的事情說給他聽。我們一起試著安排順序，遇到不清楚的地方就先停下來討論。讀到不懂的地方，我先看看前後的句子，再向老師請教。老師沒有立刻給答案，而是請我說出自己的想法。我慢慢發現，圖片和文字可以一起幫助理解故事。借書時，我用雙手把書放好，沒有折起書角。下次來，我還想找一本介紹動物的書。回家以後，我在本子上補了新的記錄。這個小小的發現，讓普通的一天變得有趣。大家笑了。我沒有急著回答，而是照著事情發生的順序慢慢回想。我仔細看了看身邊的環境。大家輪流分享，沒有人急著搶話。我記住了。這些小小的進步讓我知道，練習不是一次就要做好，而是每次都比以前多懂一點。',0,N'advanced',0),
