(1157,14,N'ZH-LONG-10-P1 · 第1段',N'今天，班上來了一位新同學。老師介紹他的名字，請大家和他問好。我帶他看看教室，也告訴他書本放在哪裡。下課時，他站在座位旁邊，不知道可以做什麼。我邀請他一起到操場玩，其他朋友也走過來介紹自己。放學以前，他笑著說，明天還想和我們一起玩。午餐時，我先問他想坐在哪裡，沒有替他做決定。他說自己喜歡畫畫，我就介紹也喜歡畫畫的朋友給他認識。有些班上的規則他還不清楚，我慢慢說明，讓他有時間發問。我發現，幫忙不只是說很多話，也要聽見別人的需要。我們不急著完成每一件事。我沒有急著回答，而是照著事情發生的順序慢慢回想。我記住了。大家一起想辦法。原來，只要多留意一點，就能在日常生活裡找到值得記住的小事。事情做好以後，我的心情也變好了。我把這件事記在本子上。大家互相了解，教室就更像一個溫暖的家。',0,N'advanced',0),
(1158,14,N'ZH-LONG-10-P2 · 第2段',N'午餐時，我先問他想坐在哪裡，沒有替他做決定。他說自己喜歡畫畫，我就介紹也喜歡畫畫的朋友給他認識。有些班上的規則他還不清楚，我慢慢說明，讓他有時間發問。我發現，幫忙不只是說很多話，也要聽見別人的需要。大家互相了解，教室就更像一個溫暖的家。我把幫助新同學的經過記在本子上，想想哪裡做得好，哪裡可以再改進。家人聽完以後，請我先說說最難忘的地方。我沒有急著回答，而是照著事情發生的順序慢慢回想。原來，只要多留意一點，就能在日常生活裡找到值得記住的小事。後來，我和朋友討論遇到問題時可以怎麼做。我們先把不同的想法說出來，再看看哪些方法適合當時的情況。有些事情需要大人的協助，有些小事則可以自己練習。這讓我很開心。朋友認真聽我說。大家不一定有相同的答案，但都願意聽完別人的理由。',0,N'advanced',0),
(1159,14,N'ZH-LONG-10-P3 · 第3段',N'幾天以後，我又想起幫助新同學的經驗。這次，我先準備好需要的東西，也提醒自己留意安全。朋友問我為什麼這樣做，我就把前一次學到的事情說給他聽。我們一起試著安排順序，遇到不清楚的地方就先停下來討論。午餐時，我先問他想坐在哪裡，沒有替他做決定。他說自己喜歡畫畫，我就介紹也喜歡畫畫的朋友給他認識。有些班上的規則他還不清楚，我慢慢說明，讓他有時間發問。我發現，幫忙不只是說很多話，也要聽見別人的需要。大家互相了解，教室就更像一個溫暖的家。回家以後，我在本子上補了新的記錄。這讓我很開心。我想把今天的發現告訴家人。我也說出自己的想法。我記住了。我們先做好準備，再開始行動。大家笑了。大家輪流分享，沒有人急著搶話。這些小小的進步讓我知道，練習不是一次就要做好，而是每次都比以前多懂一點。',0,N'advanced',0),
(1160,14,N'ZH-LONG-10 · 全文',N'今天，班上來了一位新同學。老師介紹他的名字，請大家和他問好。我帶他看看教室，也告訴他書本放在哪裡。下課時，他站在座位旁邊，不知道可以做什麼。我邀請他一起到操場玩，其他朋友也走過來介紹自己。放學以前，他笑著說，明天還想和我們一起玩。午餐時，我先問他想坐在哪裡，沒有替他做決定。他說自己喜歡畫畫，我就介紹也喜歡畫畫的朋友給他認識。有些班上的規則他還不清楚，我慢慢說明，讓他有時間發問。我發現，幫忙不只是說很多話，也要聽見別人的需要。我們不急著完成每一件事。我沒有急著回答，而是照著事情發生的順序慢慢回想。我記住了。大家一起想辦法。原來，只要多留意一點，就能在日常生活裡找到值得記住的小事。事情做好以後，我的心情也變好了。我把這件事記在本子上。大家互相了解，教室就更像一個溫暖的家。

午餐時，我先問他想坐在哪裡，沒有替他做決定。他說自己喜歡畫畫，我就介紹也喜歡畫畫的朋友給他認識。有些班上的規則他還不清楚，我慢慢說明，讓他有時間發問。我發現，幫忙不只是說很多話，也要聽見別人的需要。大家互相了解，教室就更像一個溫暖的家。我把幫助新同學的經過記在本子上，想想哪裡做得好，哪裡可以再改進。家人聽完以後，請我先說說最難忘的地方。我沒有急著回答，而是照著事情發生的順序慢慢回想。原來，只要多留意一點，就能在日常生活裡找到值得記住的小事。後來，我和朋友討論遇到問題時可以怎麼做。我們先把不同的想法說出來，再看看哪些方法適合當時的情況。有些事情需要大人的協助，有些小事則可以自己練習。這讓我很開心。朋友認真聽我說。大家不一定有相同的答案，但都願意聽完別人的理由。

幾天以後，我又想起幫助新同學的經驗。這次，我先準備好需要的東西，也提醒自己留意安全。朋友問我為什麼這樣做，我就把前一次學到的事情說給他聽。我們一起試著安排順序，遇到不清楚的地方就先停下來討論。午餐時，我先問他想坐在哪裡，沒有替他做決定。他說自己喜歡畫畫，我就介紹也喜歡畫畫的朋友給他認識。有些班上的規則他還不清楚，我慢慢說明，讓他有時間發問。我發現，幫忙不只是說很多話，也要聽見別人的需要。大家互相了解，教室就更像一個溫暖的家。回家以後，我在本子上補了新的記錄。這讓我很開心。我想把今天的發現告訴家人。我也說出自己的想法。我記住了。我們先做好準備，再開始行動。大家笑了。大家輪流分享，沒有人急著搶話。這些小小的進步讓我知道，練習不是一次就要做好，而是每次都比以前多懂一點。',0,N'advanced',0),
(1161,15,N'EN-LONG-01-P1 · 第1段',N'I get up when the sky is light. I wash my face and put on my clothes. My bag is next to the door. I check my book and my water bottle. We eat breakfast together. I walk to school with Dad. We stop before we cross the road. My friend waves to me at the gate. I put my bag beside my chair. Now I am ready to learn. Our teacher asks us to share one small thing from the morning. I tell her about a bird near our window. My friend tells us about his new shoes. We listen while each person speaks. After class, I help put the books in a neat pile. Small jobs are easier when we work together. I want to remember my water bottle again tomorrow. At home, I think about what happened. I write a few lines in my notebook. I put the events in order so that I can tell the story clearly. My family listens and asks what I learned. I explain the part that was easy and the part that was hard. We think of a small change that could help next time. I do not have to get everything right at once. Learning takes time, and I can improve by trying again. Before bed, I get ready for the next day. We talk. I tell my family about it. We help each other. There is no need to rush. We feel happy. My friend listens. A small job can teach me to be patient and to pay attention. I can use a picture to help me remember the order of the events. My family gives me time to explain what I have learned from this experience. I feel glad that I noticed something useful in an ordinary day.',0,N'advanced',0),
(1162,15,N'EN-LONG-01-P2 · 第2段',N'Our teacher asks us to share one small thing from the morning. I tell her about a bird near our window. My friend tells us about his new shoes. We listen while each person speaks. After class, I help put the books in a neat pile. Small jobs are easier when we work together. I want to remember my water bottle again tomorrow. Later, my teacher asks us to talk about a useful habit. I choose the experience from this story. Before speaking, I make a short list of what happened first and what happened next. My friend listens and asks a question. I answer with a real example instead of trying to use difficult words. We take turns so that everyone has time to speak. I learn that a clear story can help another person understand an idea. After our talk, we write down one thing we want to practise. We choose something small enough to do ourselves. If we need help, we can ask an adult. We do not pretend to know an answer when we are unsure. A careful question can be a good way to begin. At the end of class, we look at our notes again. I see that we had different ideas but could still work together. My friend listens. I put my bag beside my chair. We give each person a turn and make sure that no one feels left out. I notice that a careful plan can make a simple task easier for everyone. I can use a picture to help me remember the order of the events. I want to try this again tomorrow. My family gives me time to explain what I have learned from this experience. I put my notebook in my bag and thank my friend for listening.',0,N'advanced',0),
(1163,15,N'EN-LONG-01-P3 · 第3段',N'I get up when the sky is light. I wash my face and put on my clothes. My bag is next to the door. I check my book and my water bottle. We eat breakfast together. I walk to school with Dad. We stop before we cross the road. My friend waves to me at the gate. I put my bag beside my chair. Now I am ready to learn. A week later, I look at my notes again. Some details make me smile because I had almost forgotten them. I compare what I planned with what I actually did. One part went well, and another part needs more practice. My family asks me to choose just one change for next time. I decide to slow down, check what I need, and ask when something is unclear. My friend makes a different choice. We agree that both plans can be useful. There is no need for everyone to learn in exactly the same way. We promise to tell each other how the next try goes. I draw a small picture beside my notes. It reminds me that learning can happen outside a classroom too. A simple day can teach us how to notice, listen, plan, and care for other people. I close my notebook and put it away. We give each person a turn and make sure that no one feels left out. A small job can teach me to be patient and to pay attention. We check our work together. I notice that a careful plan can make a simple task easier for everyone. I want to remember my water bottle again tomorrow. The next time I try, I will remember to stop and think before I act. We help each other. Tomorrow will bring another chance to practise.',0,N'advanced',0),
