(1177,15,N'EN-LONG-05-P1 · 第1段',N'It starts to rain when school ends. I put on my raincoat and keep my bag dry. There is water on the path. I walk slowly and watch where I step. At the road, I stop and look for cars. Dad waits for me near our door. He has a dry towel in his hands. I change my wet shoes at home. Then I listen to the rain by the window. My friend wants to tell me a story, but the rain gets heavier. We decide to talk at school tomorrow. I hold my umbrella so that I can see in front of me. At home, I put it where no one will trip over it. I check that my books are dry. Dad says that getting home safely is more important than getting home quickly. At home, I think about what happened. I write a few lines in my notebook. I put the events in order so that I can tell the story clearly. My family listens and asks what I learned. I explain the part that was easy and the part that was hard. We think of a small change that could help next time. I do not have to get everything right at once. Learning takes time, and I can improve by trying again. Before bed, I get ready for the next day. I take my time. I tell my family about it. I remember this day. We give each person a turn and make sure that no one feels left out. My family gives me time to explain what I have learned from this experience. There is no need to rush. I do not need difficult words to tell other people about my day. I feel glad that I noticed something useful in an ordinary day.',0,N'advanced',0),
