(1189,15,N'EN-LONG-08-P1 · 第1段',N'We play with a ball after class. First we agree on the rules. Then we make two teams. I pass the ball to my friend. She catches it and passes it to another child. Once I miss the ball and feel sad. My friend says that I can try again. I take a breath and stand ready. At the end, we put the ball away together. I thank my friends for the game. Before I pass, I check that my friend is ready. I slow down and look at where I want the ball to go. Another child asks to join us. We change the teams so everyone can play. Winning is fun, but helping each other is fun too. We stop for water in the shade. Then we decide whether to play again. At home, I think about what happened. I write a few lines in my notebook. I put the events in order so that I can tell the story clearly. My family listens and asks what I learned. I explain the part that was easy and the part that was hard. We think of a small change that could help next time. I do not have to get everything right at once. Learning takes time, and I can improve by trying again. Before bed, I get ready for the next day. I look around me. I do not need difficult words to tell other people about my day. We make a plan. I notice that a careful plan can make a simple task easier for everyone. I can use a picture to help me remember the order of the events. We give each person a turn and make sure that no one feels left out. I feel glad that I noticed something useful in an ordinary day.',0,N'advanced',0),
